Source: @DISTRO_ID@-gdk-pixbuf-compat
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: @DISTRO_HOME_URL@
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: @DISTRO_ID@-gdk-pixbuf-compat
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0
Provides: libgdk-pixbuf2.0-0 (= 2.44.8)
Description: Old package name of the GdkPixbuf library, for Mojang's Minecraft launcher
 Ubuntu renamed the GdkPixbuf image-loading library's package from
 libgdk-pixbuf2.0-0 to libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0 and no longer provides the old
 name. Mojang's Minecraft.deb still depends on the old name, so apt refuses
 to install it. This empty package depends on the library under its
 current name and provides the old one, the way Ubuntu's own transitional
 packages bridge a rename.
 .
 The @DISTRO_NAME@ desktop's Install > Gaming > Minecraft installs it before
 Mojang's package.
